# Simplebeacon scan workflow (paid)

When the **simplebeacon** MCP server is available, follow this closed loop. All scans are local; do not upload source.

## 1. Before accepting generated edits

Call **`scan_snippet`** with `content` + `filePath`.

If `blockingCount > 0`:
1. Call **`propose_fix`** with `patternId`, `filePath`, `line`
2. Apply the patch (or manual fix from `manualSteps`)
3. Call **`verify_fix`** with updated content and `blockingCountBefore`
4. Call **`agent_status`** for `nextAction`

Use **`explain_finding`** when the pattern id is unclear.

## 2. After editing a file

Call **`scan_file`** on the changed path. Update session via **`agent_status`**.

## 3. Before PR / merge

1. **`scan_staged`** — gate scan on git staged files only
2. **`gate_status`** + **`suggest_fixes`**
3. CLI backstop: `npx simplebeacon scan --gate --offline --format json --output .simplebeacon/report.json`

Read `.simplebeacon/agent-brief.md` when present.

Never brag about raw finding counts; focus on gate-blocking issues.
